From a88f8f54e6bc08c6c67a7363270de0834c9b6566 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 15:43:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 63/71] eebbk: enable the container features Droidspaces asks
 for

Droidspaces v6.5.0's requirement check reported PID namespace, IPC namespace
and devtmpfs as missing (user namespace optional):

* PID_NS and IPC_NS are required.  IPC_NS depends on (SYSVIPC || POSIX_MQUEUE),
  and this config had both off, which is why the IPC namespace was missing as
  well -- so SYSVIPC, SYSVIPC_SYSCTL, POSIX_MQUEUE and POSIX_MQUEUE_SYSCTL are
  enabled too.
* DEVTMPFS=y for its "hardware access mode".  DEVTMPFS_MOUNT stays off on
  purpose: Android's init mounts its own tmpfs on /dev, and an automounted
  devtmpfs there would fight with it; CONFIG_DEVTMPFS=y is enough for a
  "mount -t devtmpfs" inside a container.
* USER_NS=y for --allow-userns.

NAMESPACES, UTS_NS, NET_NS, CGROUPS, MEMCG and SECCOMP were already enabled.
Both h130_debug.config and h130_release.config get the same block.

Checked before the full build by compiling only the affected objects
(kernel/nsproxy.c, kernel/pid*.c, kernel/user_namespace.c, ipc/*, fs/namespace.c,
fs/proc/namespaces.c, drivers/base/devtmpfs.c, kernel/cgroup/*) -- no errors.

Signed-off-by: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 EEBBK_S6_changes.md                    | 68 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 arch/arm64/configs/h130_debug.config   | 21 ++++++++
 arch/arm64/configs/h130_release.config | 21 ++++++++
 3 files changed, 110 insertions(+)

